{
  "_meta": {
    "synthetic": true,
    "notes": "SYNTHETIC. The other end of the ignition budget. A hypergolic pressure-fed service engine relights without limit, which RealFuels stores as the sentinel -1 rather than as a large count, and the section says UNLIMITED rather than showing the raw number (a '-1 LEFT' readout would be the exact failure the derived flags exist to prevent). It is also NOT SUBJECT to ullage: hypergolics settle themselves, so there is no stability to report and the row says so. A settled reading here would be a claim the Uplink cannot support, and it would look identical to a good one."
  },
